{
	"info": {
		"_postman_id": "b2c3d4e5-f6a7-4b8c-9d0e-1f2a3b4c5d6e",
		"name": "Arbiter — End-to-End: Case → Classification → Decision",
		"description": "Exercises the real cross-module flow:\n\n1. **POST** a case to cases-service (multipart: `case` JSON part + optional `documents`), which persists it and calls classification-service.\n2. **GET** the case — poll until classification resolves.\n3. **POST** the analyst's decision (APROBAR / RECHAZAR) → transitions to APPROVED / REJECTED.\n\n**State machine**:\n- `PENDING_CLASSIFICATION` → classification runs (scheduler polls every 5s)\n- `PENDING_ANALYST_REVIEW` → analyst must act (FAST_TRACK / LLM result available)\n- `AWAITING_DOCUMENTATION` → insured must upload missing docs (FALTA_DOCUMENTACION)\n- `APPROVED` / `REJECTED` → final, set by analyst decision\n\n**Requirements**: both `cases-service` (port 8083) and `classification-service` (port 8082) up.\n\n**Mock policies** (from classification-service's MockInsurerAdapter):\n- POL-001 (insuredId 12345678) — Asegurado de prueba, sum insured 500.000\n- POL-CEL-2024-001 (insuredId 40.123.456) — Laura Fernández, sum insured 400.000, 0 prior claims\n- POL-CEL-2025-099 (insuredId 30.555.777) — Marcelo Gómez, sum insured 1.200.000, 3 prior claims\n- POL-CEL-2026-042 (insuredId 42.987.654) — Sofía Martínez, sum insured 1.300.000, 0 prior claims\n\n**Scenario 5 — FALTA_DOCUMENTACION**: crea un caso de robo SIN adjuntar denuncia policial. Las reglas mock para 'Robo' requieren `police_report` + `item_photo`, así que la clasificación devuelve FALTA_DOCUMENTACION → el caso queda en `AWAITING_DOCUMENTATION`. Luego se suben los documentos faltantes vía POST /{id}/documents, el caso vuelve a `PENDING_CLASSIFICATION`, y al re-clasificarse llega a `PENDING_ANALYST_REVIEW`.\n\n**Scenario 6 — Decisión del analista**: aprueba el caso 1 (Fast Track) y rechaza el caso 3 (reincidente).",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
	},
